  "plain": "On a show hosted by a podcaster named Jesse Michels, a man named Bob Maguire, described as a CIA contractor, says that scientists working on gravity in the 1950s suddenly went quiet. He says the physicist Louis Witten did nothing more on gravity, and the inventor T. Townsend Brown went to work for the military and the companies that supply it and never published about his work again. The point he draws is that gravity research may have gone secret because it was getting somewhere."
